Article 5 (Precautions concerning Recording and Filming Activities)
(1) When granting permission under Article 4, the presiding judge shall impose the following restrictions: <Amended on December 29, 2006; and August 4, 2017.>
1. Recording or filming activities shall be limited to the period before commencement of the trial or oral arguments, or to the time of pronouncement of judgment;
2. No recording or filming activities shall be conducted on the judicial bench;
3. Recording or filming activities shall not cause a disturbance;
4. Recording or filming activities involving a defendant in custody shall be conducted after handcuffs or similar restraints have been removed;
5. Recording or filming activities involving a juvenile shall not be conducted in a manner that permits the juvenile to be identified from the name, age, occupation, appearance or other characteristics.
(2) To protect the right to present arguments, the right of defense and other rights of persons involved in litigation, maintain courtroom order, or serve the public interest, the presiding judge may take necessary measures, including limiting the time and method of recording or filming activities or attaching conditions to permission. <Newly Inserted on August 4, 2017.>
